\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Illustrative privacy-utility trade-off for a differentially-private tabular generator. As the epsilon budget widens (moving right, weaker privacy), downstream-model accuracy rises toward the no-DP ceiling, but so does the re-identification risk an audit would recover (membership-inference AUC). The two curves rise together, which is the whole difficulty: tightening privacy costs utility, and buying utility costs privacy. Numbers are illustrative, not measured.}}{149}{figure.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-privacy-utility}{{6.2}{149}{Illustrative privacy-utility trade-off for a differentially-private tabular generator. As the epsilon budget widens (moving right, weaker privacy), downstream-model accuracy rises toward the no-DP ceiling, but so does the re-identification risk an audit would recover (membership-inference AUC). The two curves rise together, which is the whole difficulty: tightening privacy costs utility, and buying utility costs privacy. Numbers are illustrative, not measured}{figure.caption.21}{}}
