\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.2}{\ignorespaces Illustrative. Probability that a whole task is correct as a function of the number of sequential tool calls it requires, under two regimes: an unverified loop with per-step reliability 0.95, and a loop with verification gates that lift the effective per-step reliability to 0.99. The curves are \(p^{n}\); they are illustrative, not measured. The gap widens with task length, which is why long agent runs need verification at the boundaries rather than a single check at the end.}}{188}{figure.caption.25}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-compounding-error}{{8.2}{188}{Illustrative. Probability that a whole task is correct as a function of the number of sequential tool calls it requires, under two regimes: an unverified loop with per-step reliability 0.95, and a loop with verification gates that lift the effective per-step reliability to 0.99. The curves are \(p^{n}\); they are illustrative, not measured. The gap widens with task length, which is why long agent runs need verification at the boundaries rather than a single check at the end}{figure.caption.25}{}}
