\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10.1}{\ignorespaces From a benchmark score to fitness for a specific deployment. The four evaluation families are cumulative, not interchangeable. A static benchmark (high internal validity on the test itself, weak external validity to any given deployment) filters the field; a task-based suite selects within it; human and subgroup review test whether the choice holds across populations; adversarial stress testing probes the remainder. The named benchmarks are illustrative, included for concreteness.}}{219}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-eval-taxonomy}{{10.1}{219}{From a benchmark score to fitness for a specific deployment. The four evaluation families are cumulative, not interchangeable. A static benchmark (high internal validity on the test itself, weak external validity to any given deployment) filters the field; a task-based suite selects within it; human and subgroup review test whether the choice holds across populations; adversarial stress testing probes the remainder. The named benchmarks are illustrative, included for concreteness}{figure.caption.28}{}}
