\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13.1}{\ignorespaces The customisation ladder as a decision tree. Rungs are ordered by cost and by the volume of labelled data required, from prompting at the bottom to continued pretraining at the top. The gate at each rung is the same: climb only if the rung below fails the team's evaluation suite. Note that a shortfall of facts sends the researcher back to the retrieval corpus rather than up to a fine-tune, and that a full fine-tune is warranted only when a parameter-efficient adapter is insufficient and labelled data are plentiful.}}{280}{figure.caption.36}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-customisation-ladder}{{13.1}{280}{The customisation ladder as a decision tree. Rungs are ordered by cost and by the volume of labelled data required, from prompting at the bottom to continued pretraining at the top. The gate at each rung is the same: climb only if the rung below fails the team's evaluation suite. Note that a shortfall of facts sends the researcher back to the retrieval corpus rather than up to a fine-tune, and that a full fine-tune is warranted only when a parameter-efficient adapter is insufficient and labelled data are plentiful}{figure.caption.36}{}}
