\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {13.1}{\ignorespaces Customisation and post-training techniques compared. The methods are ordered roughly by cost and by the labeled data they require. Prompting and RAG train no parameters at all and belong at the bottom of the ladder; the preference-alignment methods (RLHF, DPO) and continued pretraining sit at the top and are seldom in scope for teams that use rather than build models.}}{286}{table.13.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tbl-customisation-methods}{{13.1}{286}{Customisation and post-training techniques compared. The methods are ordered roughly by cost and by the labeled data they require. Prompting and RAG train no parameters at all and belong at the bottom of the ladder; the preference-alignment methods (RLHF, DPO) and continued pretraining sit at the top and are seldom in scope for teams that use rather than build models}{table.13.1}{}}
