\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13.2}{\ignorespaces Illustrative trainable-parameter counts for four customisation methods applied to a seven-billion-parameter base model, on a log scale. LoRA and QLoRA train the same small set of parameters (QLoRA's saving is in memory, not in parameter count), a few million against the roughly seven billion of a full fine-tune. The gap of three to four orders of magnitude is why parameter-efficient methods dominate when a behavior gap must be closed on modest hardware. Counts are illustrative and vary with adapter rank, targeted modules, and base size.}}{289}{figure.caption.37}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig-trainable-params}{{13.2}{289}{Illustrative trainable-parameter counts for four customisation methods applied to a seven-billion-parameter base model, on a log scale. LoRA and QLoRA train the same small set of parameters (QLoRA's saving is in memory, not in parameter count), a few million against the roughly seven billion of a full fine-tune. The gap of three to four orders of magnitude is why parameter-efficient methods dominate when a behavior gap must be closed on modest hardware. Counts are illustrative and vary with adapter rank, targeted modules, and base size}{figure.caption.37}{}}
